---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Barcode API Pricing | BarcodeNest" description="Barcode API plans from $9.99/month: 2,000 calls on Starter or 5,000 on Growth. Compare limits, annual billing, and coverage before upgrading." current="pricing">
  <header class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="eyebrow">Developer pricing</div><h1>Choose a barcode API plan for your application.</h1><p class="lede">Evaluate your catalog on Free, then choose Starter or Growth for higher monthly volume and request rates. Paid plans start at $9.99/month.</p></div></header>
  <section class="section"><div class="container">
    <div class="pricing-switcher billing-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Pricing cadence"><button class="is-active" type="button" data-pricing-toggle="month" aria-pressed="true">Monthly</button><button type="button" data-pricing-toggle="year" aria-pressed="false">Yearly <span>Save 20%</span></button></div>
    <div class="pricing-grid">
    <article class="plan"><span class="plan-tag">Evaluate coverage</span><h3>Free</h3><div class="price">$0</div><ul><li>250 lifetime successful-result credits</li><li>30 requests / minute</li><li>Single and batch barcode lookups</li><li>Dashboard and key management</li></ul><a class="button button-signal" href="/register">Get API Key</a></article>
    <article class="plan featured"><span class="plan-tag">Starter · Small integrations</span><h3>Starter</h3><p>2,000 API calls / month</p><div class="price" data-monthly="$9.99|/ month" data-yearly="$7.99|/ month">$9.99 <small>/ month</small></div><p class="annual-total" hidden>Billed $95.90 yearly</p><ul><li>300 requests / minute</li><li>Monthly usage tracking</li><li>API key management</li><li>Email support</li></ul><a class="button button-signal" data-paid-plan="STARTER" href="/billing/?plan=STARTER&amp;interval=month">Choose Starter</a></article>
    <article class="plan"><span class="plan-tag">Growth · More volume</span><h3>Growth</h3><p>5,000 API calls / month</p><div class="price" data-monthly="$19.99|/ month" data-yearly="$15.99|/ month">$19.99 <small>/ month</small></div><p class="annual-total" hidden>Billed $191.90 yearly</p><ul><li>1,200 requests / minute</li><li>Monthly usage tracking</li><li>API key management</li><li>Email support</li></ul><a class="button" data-paid-plan="GROWTH" href="/billing/?plan=GROWTH&amp;interval=month">Choose Growth</a></article>
  </div><div class="callout"><strong>Usage accounting:</strong> Free accounts receive 250 lifetime credits: each matched barcode result consumes one credit, including each matched result in a batch. Existing recorded usage counts toward the lifetime allowance. Paid plans count valid single lookup attempts and each submitted batch barcode as one unit, including missing products. Authentication failures, health checks, and account pages do not consume allowance. Failed lookups consume no Free credits. Annual subscriptions are billed yearly; API allowances reset monthly.</div></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="narrow"><h2>Which plan fits your workload?</h2><p>Use Free to validate a representative sample. Choose Starter when you need up to 2,000 monthly lookups or a higher request rate than Free. Choose Growth for up to 5,000 monthly lookups or bursts up to 1,200 requests/minute. All tiers use the same product index; upgrading increases allowances, not product coverage.</p><p>For example, 1,000 successful single-product requests use 1,000 paid calls. Each submitted barcode consumes one paid lookup unit.</p><h2>How do I buy a paid plan?</h2><p>Choose Starter or Growth above, sign in or create an account, and review the selected plan in Billing. Payment starts only when you explicitly continue to secure checkout.</p><h2>What should I check before upgrading?</h2><p>Test coverage and required fields with your actual products. Review <a href="/data/">data sources</a> and <a href="/terms/">data-use terms</a>. Product matches, images, and field completeness vary. For workflows, see <a href="/barcode-api-for-inventory/">inventory integrations</a> and <a href="/product-data-api/">catalog enrichment</a>.</p><h2>Need more than 5,000 calls per month?</h2><p><a href="/contact/">Contact us with your expected monthly volume and request rate</a> before choosing a plan.</p></div></section>
  <section class="cta-band"><div class="container cta-grid"><div><div class="eyebrow">Free developer tier</div><h2>Create your account and make the first request.</h2></div><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-signal" href="/register">Get Free API Key</a><a class="button" href="/docs">Documentation</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
<script>
  type Interval = "month" | "year";
  function selectPricing(interval: Interval) {
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-pricing-toggle]").forEach((button) => { const active = button.dataset.pricingToggle === interval; button.classList.toggle("is-active", active); button.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(active)); });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".price[data-monthly]").forEach((price) => { const [amount, cadence] = (interval === "year" ? price.dataset.yearly : price.dataset.monthly)!.split("|"); price.innerHTML = `${amount} <small>${cadence}</small>`; });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>("[data-paid-plan]").forEach((link) => { link.href = `/billing/?plan=${link.dataset.paidPlan}&interval=${interval}`; });
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>(".annual-total").forEach((note) => note.hidden = interval !== "year");
  }
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-pricing-toggle]").forEach((button) => button.addEventListener("click", () => selectPricing(button.dataset.pricingToggle as Interval)));
</script>
